# From "Exploration, Sleep" (Wave I - Discovery, CD3-5). Unlike most F10
# tools, this one is meant to end in actual sleep, not a return count -- a
# session using it should end @ending stay, or simply let the listener drift.
# The transcript's countdown (11-20) has three ASR number errors -- "sixty",
# "seventy", "ninety" for sixteen/seventeen/nineteen, and a garbled "twenty
# twenty twenty" -- corrected here against the stated 11-to-20 sequence.

@segment   exploration-sleep
@title     Exploration — Sleep
@levels    F10
@duration  ~3m

say From Focus 10, explore the process your body uses to fall into total sleep — a way to remember what that feels like, so you can call on it later.
pause 8
say Think how nice it would be to float. To float out and away. Calm. Serene.
pause 8
say Turn slowly, as if you were a log rolling in water.
pause 6
say Detach easily. Let yourself float upward, slowly, up and away. Calm and pleasant.
pause 10
say Notice how you feel right now. Remember it.
pause 8
say Now float back down, in the direction you came from. More, and more.
pause 8
say Turn again, as if you were a log rolling in water.
pause 6
say You're nearly back where you started.
pause 5
say Now you've returned, completely, to where you began.
pause 6
say Relax, and feel calm and comfortable in Focus 10. Remember what you've noticed.
pause 8
say From this moment on, whenever you want normal, natural, restful sleep, count slowly in your mind from one to twenty. When you reach twenty, you'll be there.
pause 10
say The more you use this, the easier and more effective it becomes.
pause 6
say Let this count carry the rest of the way. Eleven. Twelve. Thirteen. Fourteen. Fifteen. Sixteen. Seventeen. Eighteen. Nineteen. Twenty.
hold 60
